---
title: Uses
---
# Hardware

## Gaming PC

- GPU: Zotac RTX 5080 AMP EXTREME Infinity 16GB
- CPU: Ryzen 7 7800X3D w/ DeepCool 360mm AIO
- Monitor: ASUS ROG Strix XG27UCDMG, 26.5" 3840x2160 240Hz
- RAM: 32GB DDR5 G.Skill Z5
- Case: NZXT H9 Flow
- Power supply: Cooler Master 850W
- OS's: Dual boot Windows 11 | EndeavorOS Hyprland & Plasma 6

## Peripherals

- Keyboard: Womier RD75 keyboard - I've changed keyboards a lot over the years. I don't like this one as much as I should. Probably gonna change eventually.
- Mouse: Glorious Model O3 Wireless mouse - Personally I love the hot-swappable batteries.
- Gaming headset: Audeze Maxwell headphones - I'm not crazy about these either. They give me neck pain after a couple hours. Sound quality is great, though I do miss my Steelseries Arctis Pro Wireless.
- Work headset: Shokz OpenFit Pro - Comfortable, open-ear, great sound quality. Bad Bluetooth latency.
- Microphone: Blue Yeti mic - Have had this for over a decade, no issues, fantastic quality.
- Controller: Steam Controller - Just got this :) love the trackpads. Great with my Steam Deck.

## Other devices/PCs

- Raspberry Pi 5 with Pironman 5 case
  - The case comes with a NVMe SSD hat, which I put a 256GB SSD in when the ram prices weren't crazy. It acts as my personal cloud server. I used to run a vanilla Minecraft server with okay performance on it, but I since shut it down.
  - Now it hosts my personal [landing page](https://github.com/bdelucia/landing-page) website as well as being my synced cloud storage for both emulation game saves and my personal Obsidian vault. This thing is awesome and I'm glad I found a great use case for it.
- Steam Deck, 512TB OLED
  - I love this thing to death. It was pretty much an instant buy when I heard it was running off of an Arch-based OS. It's an absolute dream.
  - This allowed me to play games I never would've played before, like *Breath of the Wild* and *Super Mario Odyssey.*
  - It also emulates Gamecube and Wii U like a dream.
- Lenovo Legion 5 laptop
  - This is my personal laptop, I don't have anything crazy. I got this for use at ASU, I didn't want to bring my whole gaming setup so I brought this laptop.
  - It has a GTX 1660 Ti mobile… which in 2020 was okay but is meh now. The 5.0Ghz (when boosted), 6-core Intel i7-10750H is great for gaming though. I don't game at all on this thing anymore though.
  - Have it dual booted the same way my Gaming PC is… dual boot Windows 11 & EndeavorOS Hyprland.
- Google Pixel 10 Pro XL
  - Switched to this after over 8 years with the iPhone 8 Plus. I like it.
  - It does allow me to do Android-specific stuff like Syncthing with Obsidian, and Gemini seems to be more useful than Siri.
  - Not completely convinced of Android just yet.

# Software

## General productivity

- Firefox - I've used all of the main browsers, Edge, Chromium, Opera GX, Brave, and Arc. Firefox has been my favorite, not for any particular reasons, just feels nice to use and I have used it all my life. Chromium is a close 2nd.
- 1Password - Just started using this, and it is honestly worth it for $5 a month. Saves so much time logging in and gives me peace of mind knowing my passwords are secure as possible, and all different from one another. I hate subscriptions but I don't mind paying for this one.
- Obsidian - I have a personal vault synced between my PCs, with my Raspberry Pi 5 acting as the cloud server. Its beautiful, local, quick and useful. I have a whole repo about my Obsidian setup you can find [here](https://github.com/bdelucia/obsidian-customizations).

## Cursor/VSCode setup

- Theme: Dark Modern - Yeah I know. It's a default theme. I like it though. No community theme has ever impressed me. Dark Modern "just works".
- Font: CaskaydiaCove Nerd Font. - This allows me to see all the icons in my custom WSL2 Terminal. It's also the mono font for my personal design system
- File Icon Theme: Bearded Icons - Simple, Boxicons-like
- Product Icon Theme: Fluent Icons - These go nicely with Bearded Icons.
- Extensions:
  - Error Lens - This is pretty nice, coworker had it and I liked the instant feedback from it.
  - VSCode Pets - Also saw this on one of my coworker's IDE. It's cute.
  - vscode-pdf - I don't use this often, but when I don't have it I notice it. It's a feature I wish vanilla VSCode had.
  - Markdown Editor - Nice to preview what something looks like in Markdown. I don't use the WYSIWYG editor all that much.

## Development

- Neovim - I use this all the time for editing local files on my EndeavorOS systems. Makes vim feel actually usable lol. I pair it with NvChad, which makes it look even better! Makes editing local files something I look forward to.
- WSL2 - I use this at work and on my Windows machines when I code there. Nice to have a zsh terminal while in Windows.
- Kitty - This is the terminal I use on my EndeavorOS systems.
- oh-my-zsh - I use this for completions, syntax highlighting, auto-suggestions and more.
- Starship.rs - I use this for terminal styling. I have a personal Starship config file that I use, you can find it [here](https://github.com/bdelucia/Starship-Config).

# Everyday stuff

- Owala FreeSip 40oz - Yes I am probably outing myself with this one. But a 40oz bottle of cold, sealed water is amazing and I use it everyday
- Optimum Nutrition 2.5g Creatine pills - I take 2 of these a day, it's easier then scooping powder and putting it in a drink.
- Sports Research Triple-Strength Omega-3 pills - I don't eat a lot of fish so I assume my Omega 3 levels are lacking.
- Magnesium glynicate - Honestly love this stuff, I'm a rough sleeper so this helps me have really deep sleep. I always dream like crazy on this stuff.
- Below Zero cooling comforter - Got this for $40 at Costco, honestly a game changer for sleeping. Especially during hot AZ summer nights.
- Robinhood Gold Card - 3% cash back across the board is crazy. Also the card is metal and golden so it is cool. All cash back goes into my Roth IRA, which gets 3% match. Nice to have another passive way to increase Roth contributions.
- Fitbit Charge 6 - Got this from my dad. Don't have a strong opinion about this, it just works.
